{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs595weuf97ME9mM2bXp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The root cause is `dedupe_rows` in `reporting/dedupe.py`. It tracked seen event IDs in a list, so every row did a linear scan, which makes the step quadratic. The refactor changed it from a set-based version, and its docstring says so. I changed it back to a set. The output is unchanged and the full suite passes.\n\n**The fix** (`reporting/dedupe.py`): `seen_ids` is now a `set()` and uses `.add()`. Rows are still kept in first-occurrence order.\n\n**Regression test** (`tests/test_dedupe.py`, new file):\n- `test_dedupe_keeps_first_occurrence_in_order` checks the ordering and first-wins behaviour.\n- `test_dedupe_lookup_does_not_scale_quadratically` counts `__eq__` calls on the IDs rather than timing anything, so it can't flake. With 3000 unique rows the old code made 4,498,500 comparisons. The test asserts fewer than 3000. It failed on the old code and passes now.\n\n**Results:**\n- Full suite: `3 passed`.\n- `build_report` on 30k rows with UUID-style IDs: about 4.55s before, 0.009s after.\n- On 30k rows with heavy duplication, the new `dedupe_rows` returns exactly the same list as the original code.\n\n**Something doesn't add up.** This is quadratic, but at 30k rows on this machine it took about 5 seconds, not an hour. Reaching an hour would take far more rows or a different data shape than the ticket describes. So this is a real root cause, but it may not be the whole story. If the ops run still crawls after this change, the next thing to check is the actual input file (row count, ID length, how many IDs are unique) and whether the nightly job runs anything else on the same path.\n\n**Not done:**\n- I did not commit. The working tree has the two source changes plus the new test file.\n- Running pytest rewrote the tracked `reporting/__pycache__/dedupe.cpython-314.pyc`, which shows as modified in git. I left it alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9938,"cache_read_input_tokens":53829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9938},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15d7c02d-90bb-4f5a-9cfe-cbce30f4b680","uuid":"42a01dbc-ca8f-4d55-b85e-c27e824141ab","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:39:28.966Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs595dKJuCt5phkjUXBR"}
